course: dictionary
lesson: 13712
title: Instantaneously: happening at once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Instantaneously is a longer way of saying instantly or at once. It tells you that something happens with no time passing in between. «The lights went out instantaneously when the power failed.» The lights did not fade or flicker first. They went off straight away.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. The word «when» links two things, and the lights changed right at that moment. If you swap in «instantly», the sentence still makes sense, so instantaneously must mean the same. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: In science, instantaneous has a special use. «Instantaneous speed» is the speed at one exact moment, like the number on a speedometer when a car passes a sign. It is not an average over a whole journey. The word points to one exact instant, not a period of time.
fact: Instantaneously is an adverb, from the adjective instantaneous.
fact: «Instantaneously» means immediately, with no time passing in between.
fact: In science, «instantaneously» can mean at one exact instant of time, rather than over a period.
fact: «Instantaneous speed» is the speed at one exact moment, like on a speedometer.
fact: «Instantly» and «at once» are simpler words with a similar meaning. You may also see «almost instantaneously» and «happen instantaneously».
exercise: «The alarm sounded instantaneously when the door opened.» What does instantaneously mean? | Slowly and quietly | After a long wait | Only sometimes | *At once, with no time passing
exercise: Which word is a simpler way of saying instantaneously? | *Instantly | Gradually | Later | Maybe
exercise: Nadia says, «The speedometer showed the car's instantaneous speed.» What does instantaneous speed mean? | The distance the car travelled | *The speed at one exact moment | The average speed over a whole journey | The speed of a snail
test: «The light from the lamp reaches your eyes almost instantaneously over short distances.» What is this saying? | *It arrives very quickly, almost at once | It never arrives | It arrives only at night | It takes many hours to arrive
test: What does a speedometer show? | The weather outside | The total distance of a journey | The number of passengers in the car | *The speed at one exact instant
exam: When Ben pressed send, the message arrived instantaneously. What does instantaneously mean here? | Never | Slowly, over a whole week | *At once, with no time passing | Only on Sundays
